1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,657
Welcome to Atomic Education.

2
00:00:02,716 --> 00:00:09,878
This lesson was written by the Atomic teaching team to help you learn Cambridge Lower Secondary Science with confidence.

3
00:00:09,878 --> 00:00:10,588
Let's begin!

4
00:00:11,647 --> 00:00:13,363
Welcome to Unit 2: Excretion.

5
00:00:14,423 --> 00:00:16,612
Your body is about 60 percent water.

6
00:00:16,612 --> 00:00:21,939
You can survive around three weeks without food, but only about three days without water!

7
00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:25,253
We lose water when we sweat and when we use the toilet.

8
00:00:25,253 --> 00:00:28,686
Which organs keep the right amount of water in our bodies?

9
00:00:29,745 --> 00:00:31,639
To excrete means to get rid of.

10
00:00:31,639 --> 00:00:37,735
Excretion removes waste products made by metabolism, the chemical reactions that keep our cells alive.

11
00:00:37,735 --> 00:00:40,280
It stops toxic substances from building up.

12
00:00:41,339 --> 00:00:47,080
Three main organs excrete. The lungs remove carbon dioxide and water vapour when we breathe out.

13
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:50,513
The skin removes water, salts and a little urea in sweat.

14
00:00:50,513 --> 00:00:54,123
And the kidneys remove excess water, salts and urea in urine.

15
00:00:55,182 --> 00:00:58,082
Urea is made when our body breaks down proteins.

16
00:00:58,082 --> 00:01:02,699
Eating more protein than we need increases the amount of urea we must excrete.

17
00:01:03,758 --> 00:01:09,025
A mirror has been kept in a fridge so it is cold. A student breathes out gently onto it.

18
00:01:09,025 --> 00:01:12,458
Predict: what will appear on the mirror? Pause and decide.

19
00:01:13,517 --> 00:01:17,009
Watch. The student breathes out slowly onto the cold glass.

20
00:01:18,068 --> 00:01:23,632
A misty patch appears. Up close, it is made of tiny droplets of water, which slowly disappear.

21
00:01:24,691 --> 00:01:30,373
Explain what you saw. Breathed-out air contains water vapour, made in our cells by respiration.

22
00:01:30,373 --> 00:01:33,983
When it touches the cold mirror, it condenses into droplets.

23
00:01:33,983 --> 00:01:39,191
So the lungs excrete water vapour as well as carbon dioxide: they are excretory organs.

24
00:01:39,191 --> 00:01:41,499
Pause and explain it in your own words.

25
00:01:42,559 --> 00:01:44,512
Urine is about 95 percent water.

26
00:01:44,512 --> 00:01:49,306
The other 5 percent is roughly 2 percent urea and 3 percent salts and uric acid.

27
00:01:49,306 --> 00:01:51,377
These figures are only approximate.

28
00:01:52,436 --> 00:01:57,053
Drink a lot of water and your urine becomes paler and you urinate more often.

29
00:01:57,053 --> 00:02:02,734
If you're dehydrated, your body conserves water, so you make less urine, and it's darker yellow.

30
00:02:03,794 --> 00:02:10,245
These are typical amounts of water lost in one day by an adult in a cool climate, who is not exercising hard.

31
00:02:11,304 --> 00:02:14,737
Most water, about one and a half litres, leaves in urine.

32
00:02:14,737 --> 00:02:19,886
About half a litre is lost as sweat, and almost half a litre in the air we breathe out.

33
00:02:20,945 --> 00:02:26,863
Pause and decide: which of these amounts would rise on a hot day, and how would the kidneys respond?

34
00:02:27,923 --> 00:02:34,314
The excretory system is made up of two kidneys in the lower back, two ureters, the bladder and the urethra.

35
00:02:34,314 --> 00:02:38,576
The renal artery and renal vein connect the kidneys to the blood supply.

36
00:02:39,635 --> 00:02:43,127
Urine flows down the ureters and is stored in the bladder.

37
00:02:43,127 --> 00:02:48,986
When it's full, you feel the need to urinate: a muscle opens and urine leaves through the urethra.

38
00:02:48,986 --> 00:02:52,715
Fun fact: wetlands filter water just like kidneys filter blood!

39
00:02:53,774 --> 00:02:56,792
Blood enters each kidney through the renal artery.

40
00:02:56,792 --> 00:03:01,172
The kidney filters out urea, excess water and excess salts to form urine.

41
00:03:01,172 --> 00:03:05,315
Clean blood, with its useful nutrients, leaves through the renal vein.

42
00:03:06,374 --> 00:03:09,688
Healthy kidneys filter about 180 litres of fluid a day!

43
00:03:09,688 --> 00:03:15,725
If they fail, patients may need dialysis, where a machine cleans their blood, or a kidney transplant.

44
00:03:15,725 --> 00:03:20,223
We can live with one kidney, and bioartificial kidneys may be ready by 2030.

45
00:03:21,282 --> 00:03:26,017
Our excretory organs work all day. Here are four ways they affect everyday life.

46
00:03:27,076 --> 00:03:32,995
During a long run you sweat a lot. Your kidneys save water, so you make less urine and it is darker.

47
00:03:34,054 --> 00:03:38,730
Pale, straw-coloured urine is a simple sign that you are drinking enough water.

48
00:03:39,789 --> 00:03:45,530
If the kidneys fail, a dialysis machine filters urea and extra water out of the patient's blood,

49
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:46,773
several times a week.

50
00:03:47,832 --> 00:03:53,987
A person can live a healthy life with only one kidney, so a living donor can give a kidney to a patient.

51
00:03:55,046 --> 00:03:58,361
Healthy kidneys keep water, salts and waste in balance.

52
00:03:58,361 --> 00:04:02,918
Pause and think: what colour should your urine be when you are well hydrated?

53
00:04:03,977 --> 00:04:09,481
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

54
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:14,861
Question 1: Name the three main organs of excretion. Pause the video now.

55
00:04:15,920 --> 00:04:17,814
Answer: Lungs, skin and kidneys.

56
00:04:18,873 --> 00:04:22,543
Question 2: What is urine mostly made of? Pause the video now.

57
00:04:23,602 --> 00:04:25,496
Answer: Water, about 95 percent.

58
00:04:26,555 --> 00:04:31,822
Question 3: Which tube carries urine from the kidney to the bladder? Pause the video now.

59
00:04:32,881 --> 00:04:34,006
Answer: The ureter.

60
00:04:35,065 --> 00:04:39,149
Question 4: Why might your urine be dark yellow? Pause the video now.

61
00:04:40,208 --> 00:04:43,404
Answer: You are dehydrated, so it contains less water.
